e A as better overall because reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh C's issues. Let's argue that.\n\nWe need to reference facts: Candidate A known 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, quick correct decisions. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Candidate C: can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized. Argue that unorganized and poor feedback orientation are more safety-critical than egocentric communication, and that reliability and crew atmosphere are crucial for long flights. So I will change vote to Candidate A.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
